  "description": "REYYEB crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P c c n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C6 H16 N1 1+,C104 H84 Dy5 Mn4 N12 O38 1-,10(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1A (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn2A (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 16 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.420-3.556 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.10-133.27°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (NHEt3)[Mn4Dy5O2(OH)4(NO3)4(saph)8(H2O)4]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
